4. Data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No ISLES'26 imaging data, ground-truth segmentation, model checkpoint or
prediction volume is distributed here, and none should ever become distributable
by accident: `.gitignore` blocks the volume and weight formats outright, and
also blocks the per-case scorer caches under `analysis/`, which are derived from
the data and carry subject identifiers even though they are only numbers.
The challenge data is obtained from the ISLES'26 organisers under their own
terms.

Two properties of that cohort are assumed by the code and are stated here
because the dataset itself is not ours to describe in detail. The pooled
out-of-fold evaluation covers 1,453 subjects. Voxel volume across that cohort
spans 0.031 to 5.27 mm^3 — a factor of roughly 170 — because ISLES'26 is
native-space and multi-site; that spread is precisely why a size threshold
expressed in voxels and one expressed in mm^3 are different filters, and it is
the reason this repository exists.
